WEBVTT

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:38.060
Arumi, you're too fast!

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.620
You're just too slow!

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.050
Sasshi!

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.890
Masa-jii!

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.560
Don't fall!

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:10.520
Papa!

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:13.200
Arumi!

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.750
Arumi! What happened to Masa-jii?!

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:35.330
It brings back memories of way back when...

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:44.350
It was a long time ago...

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:46.970
Back when we were all young.

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:50.060
Before Grill Pelican was built.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:57.110
Not only that, this is a story from so long ago...

00:02:57.110 --> 00:03:01.640
...there wasn't a bit of Abenobashi Shopping Arcade standing.

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:05.950
With this so-called urban planning...

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.620
...the shacks and open black-markets that popped up after the war...

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:10.950
...were all cleared away good and proper.

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:14.460
That left this one section of town in front of the train station...

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:19.720
...completely wide open and bare, like it had just been bombed out.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:24.170
The hair on the top of my head was still growing thick.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:28.240
Though I was scrawny and no good at fights, I was trying to be cool...

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:31.440
...and was so with the times in the belief that...

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.940
"If you're a man, you should go out there and make your mark!"

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:38.810
And I may have been a little overly eager.

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:41.700
I was the kind of youth every town had back then.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:43.780
Yo, Mune-chan.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.910
No, I was just a punk.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:51.390
Oh, Masa-bou.

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:53.130
What are you doing here in the middle of the day?

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:54.820
Did you get fired again?

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.590
Please, Mune-chan, don't call me "Masa-bou".

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:01.420
"Bou?" Come on, I'm way older than you.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:02.930
Then, should I call you Masa-jii?

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:05.500
How much older are ya trying to make me? That's going too far.

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:07.180
But never mind that...

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:11.810
I'm not here today just hanging about for no reason.

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:13.950
I'm here to do prep work and preliminary inspections...

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:15.690
...for the awesome project that's being started here.

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:16.890
You get it?

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:18.050
No.

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:19.960
I don't really care, but could you go away?

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:22.690
Mom's told me not to talk to you.

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:24.690
Yeah, that's the thing! That's exactly my point!

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:27.430
I'm trying to do something about that.

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:30.590
I'll bet your mom's probably got the wrong idea 'bout me.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.660
Look, listen to me.

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:35.640
It's a project that's been authorized by the prefectural governor of Osaka himself!

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:37.010
Isn't that something?

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:41.810
And today, I've brought an amazing and respected man here from Tokyo.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:46.110
Well, well, Osaka and Tokyo. You must be keeping the Tokaido Line busy.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:54.420
That's Abe-sensei, a specialist in urban planning.

00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:01.820
Mune-chan, as a man, I haven't really talked about this much...

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:03.660
...but I've got this little dream, see?

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:07.140
And that's to open up my own shop!

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:09.470
Not some stupid place like the cafeteria in the department store...

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:11.440
...where I'm forced to work my butt off everyday.

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:14.180
I'm talking about a place that serves serious French cooking.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.180
What do ya think?

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:18.440
And then, start a family.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:22.410
Maybe something will, you know, happen between you and me, and...

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:27.360
Like you know, all I've got to live by is a kitchen knife...

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.860
...and English and French are both gibberish to me...

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:31.830
...I can't even read a menu, ya know?

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:34.900
So, I want to have some kids quick and...

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:37.630
Well, who knows if it'll be a boy or a girl, but...

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:40.430
Well, no, it'd be better if it's a boy, wouldn't it?

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:44.570
I'll train him up and make it so he can speak some language fluently...

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:46.910
...kinda like a cosmopolitan type, who can do business all over the world.

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:49.280
I'll raise him into something like that and take advantage of that...

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:53.210
No, I'm not thinking about making him take over my shop or anything.

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:55.720
Yeah, I know, maybe I'll get him to open a second place...

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:57.520
...in Paris, France, the home of our cooking.

00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:00.490
And we'd go visit every so often to see how he's doing.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.820
Husband and wife, in the city of Paris.

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:04.560
Bon jour to the Champs-Elysees Avenue.

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:06.690
Arc de Triomphe and Yvette Giraud. But anyway...

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.500
Hey, hey, what d'you think?

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:11.590
Doesn't this plan sound great?

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:17.310
Yes, really... wonderful.

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:24.440
Sensei! Sensei! Let's hurry, let's hurry, let's hurry!

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:27.220
I don't care if it's the shopping arcade or Heiankyo, let's build it right now!

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:29.240
Where should we get started?! What should I do?!

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:31.320
I'll do anything! Shall I hold in my farts too?!

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.410
Hammering, hammering.

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:40.790
Whoa, Sensei, that is way cool!

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:44.530
This is one of those modern housing units that's so popular now, huh?

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:47.470
Sensei, are you going to be living here by yourself?

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:51.300
Yeah. I haven't gotten any furnishings yet, though.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:52.760
So, it's empty.

00:06:53.170 --> 00:06:54.940
Oh, there's another room in the back.

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:56.880
It's a room to bring the ladies home to.

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:58.080
This is great.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:58.940
Really.

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:01.650
If you need a place, I wouldn't mind lending you my key.

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:03.550
I tend to be out a lot anyway.

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:04.790
For real?!

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:06.290
You're okay with me using this place?!

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:07.290
You're sure?!

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:09.190
Yes, please, yes!

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:13.790
Oh, Sensei, you certainly understand a man's needs.

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:16.740
Well, the truth is, I've got a bit of a plan.

00:07:17.230 --> 00:07:19.570
Is there a futon in the back room? There is?

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:20.970
All right...

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:22.340
I'll use the back room...

00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:24.610
To do things like this and things like that...

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:27.370
Young blood and young bodies riding the tide...

00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:29.920
Ahem!

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:32.930
So, that's what your plan was about?

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:36.140
No, no, no! Mune-chan, you got it all wrong! All wrong!

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:38.220
I'm not thinking about anything nasty like that!

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:40.220
Totally, not one bit!

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:41.600
Nothing nasty at all!

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.610
Abenobashi Shopping Arcade?

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:48.690
Well? Are ya surprised?

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:52.090
We're not talking anything stingy like a house or a shop.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:55.670
We're building a brand new town from scratch!

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:56.780
How 'bout it?

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:05.410
Hmm, so my family's Turtle Bath is at the northern end.

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:09.250
A road going straight south and another one going east-west, with a grid pattern...

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:12.720
It's kinda like the city of Kyoto...

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:13.470
Yes!

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:16.660
This tetrapentic framework itself...

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:18.760
...will change all the yin in the atmosphere to yang.

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:21.770
It's the one and only system that will create an exquisite balance...

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:23.930
...to counter the powerful welling of the netherworld's power...

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:25.400
...which is characteristic of this region!

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:29.940
By arranging sacred beasts on all sides, east, west, north and south...

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:33.340
...this matrix will raise the chi ventilation rate to nearly 100%.

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:35.940
In addition, the true-word barriers erected at the four corners...

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:38.610
...makes the security of this place perfectly reliable.

00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:41.450
The backbone, the mainstay of this thing, will have the greatest range in the industry!

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:44.990
Compared to previously distributed products, it's an amazing 4.6 times better!

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:46.960
Through the high-speed dragon vein network, it will be possible...

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:49.990
...to have a regular connection to distant Taishan and even Kunlun.

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:54.030
The new thousand year realm bolstered by the ultimate in science and technology!

00:08:54.030 --> 00:08:56.140
That is the Abenobashi Shopping Arcade!

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:03.760
Was that Japanese?

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:06.440
What a passionate man.

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:15.820
One saurel meal, one kid's lunch!

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:16.840
Got it!

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:28.760
Even after the passage of a thousand years...

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:31.500
...the same flowers bloom in the same shape...

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:36.600
It reminds me of when we were kids. Right, Masayuki?

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:37.220
Huh?

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:40.720
What are you saying, Sensei?

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:47.730
Mune-chan, are ya going to see Abe-sensei?

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:49.810
I'm delivering his lunch.

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:52.820
That is...

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:55.160
...about the shopping arcade...

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:56.920
The parcels of land they're gonna start selling...

00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:58.070
...can anyone buy them?

00:09:58.460 --> 00:10:01.620
Yeah, I heard there's quite a few people coming in from other parts.

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:08.160
I saw Masa-bou this morning and he was awful fired up 'bout buying a plot.

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:12.460
It just made me think that in his own way, he's pretty serious 'bout this.

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:15.920
Wow, Masa-bou said that?

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:24.260
Moron! Retard! Scum! Ya better take adults seriously!

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:26.150
All right!

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:31.830
So, like I said, you can take all the interest you want on it.

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:32.480
Don't you get it?!

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:35.560
I am very sorry.

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:38.230
Why can't you lend me any money?! Tell me!

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:39.970
This is a bank, right?

00:10:39.970 --> 00:10:42.400
People entrust their money to you...

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:44.610
...you turn around, loan that money out, and skim off the top.

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:46.970
That's how a bank does business, ain't it?

00:10:46.970 --> 00:10:49.100
I am very sorry, sir.

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:51.570
Why can't you?!

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:55.480
Day after day, I work hard with sweat on my brows to earn my salary...

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:57.750
...and, okay, so it's not all of it, it's not all of it...

00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:01.450
...but I put quite a sum into the vault here every month!

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:04.630
I'm being at least a little useful to you guys too!

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:06.460
I'm right, aren't I?

00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:10.400
Thank you for making use of our savings account, sir.

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:14.070
Is that it? Don't you got anything else to say to me?!

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:16.340
I am very sorry, sir.

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:18.430
Don't you got a sympathetic bone in your body?

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:21.410
No, sir, I do not.

00:11:26.110 --> 00:11:28.410
<i>If you run into trouble, show them that business card.</i>

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:30.660
<i>It should get you through most tough spots.</i>

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:36.690
What's this?

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:39.690
Who is...

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:06.890
The effectiveness of that business card was as excellent as the ad for soap...

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:09.480
...that went "Cleans you fast! Cleans you good!"

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:14.630
Even the grim loan officer ground his forehead into the desktop...

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:17.100
...practically begging me to borrow the money.

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:19.600
At the time, I thought he was a worthless guy...

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:22.600
...for changing his attitude just like that over a scrap of paper...

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:25.970
...but now that I think back, this was the beginning...

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:28.770
...of the ultimate science that Sensei was talking about.

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:35.580
Everything's going so smoothly, it's almost creepy, Sensei.

00:12:40.350 --> 00:12:42.260
These're awfully fine chamber pots.

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:42.650
Wrong.

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:44.660
But no matter how ya look at them...

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:47.200
...they look like chamber pots that the new rich would use.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:49.530
These are devices that will serve as the linchpins of the town.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:50.800
Stickpins?

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:51.410
Linchpins!

00:12:52.430 --> 00:12:54.940
Genbu to the North, Suzaku to the South, ...

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:57.750
...Byakko to the West, and Seiryu to the East.

00:12:58.510 --> 00:13:00.940
This is in accordance with the fundamental theory behind the harmony of the four gods.

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:04.010
We will set these sacred beasts up on the roofs of the shops...

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:07.610
...that are located in each of these directions and control the flow of chi.

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:45.630
And don't you ever come near my daughter again!

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:48.620
If you do, I'll tie ya up and burn ya!

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:52.790
But Mother, haven't you heard anything from Mune-san?

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:55.850
About the date for the ceremony? Or about betrothal gifts?

00:13:59.300 --> 00:14:00.840
Well, damn it all! Wicked old hag!

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:02.390
Pig ass! Old bat!

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:18.080
Mune-chan.

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:23.960
Mune-chan, I picked out a name for my restaurant!

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:26.160
French One-Course Service, Grill Pelican!

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:28.600
What do you think? Has a nice ring to it, huh?

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:30.060
How about it, honey?

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:36.790
This tree's supposed to live for a thousand years after planting it.

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:37.850
A thousand years?

00:14:39.340 --> 00:14:41.310
That's a laurel tree.

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:45.210
There's a lot of mega big ones growing on the grounds of the Seimei Shrine...

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:46.860
...but why here?

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:49.860
That man asked me to plant one here.

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:52.680
That man?

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:04.600
So, this is for "that man," too, huh?

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:05.860
Oh, wait.

00:15:11.740 --> 00:15:12.510
I'll deliver it for ya.

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:14.100
Masa-bou!

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:21.850
"That man," my butt!

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:22.440
Pisses me off!

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:24.990
It pisses me off, so I'm gonna eat it all!

00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:29.590
This is pretty good.

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:36.200
It's so unfair, I can't stand it.

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:40.330
If you will have me...

00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:40.330
I want to be a clam.

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:42.400
You haven't even had a drop to drink.

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:43.970
I will happily...

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:44.300
How long're ya gonna sit there babbling to yourself?

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:53.210
Enter the embrace of your arms...

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:49.110
I can grumble all night long just by sitting here and staring at it.

00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:51.280
I'm saying that you're being a real nuisance!

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:53.210
What're ya bragging about? Talk about moronic.

00:15:53.210 --> 00:16:01.420
I don't know about tomorrow...

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:55.300
If you're not gonna drink anymore, I'm closing up shop!

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:59.020
Tomorrow's gonna be busy because of Seimei-san's festival.

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:03.190
That was my role...

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:07.230
I may come to hate you...

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:07.230
So, what's wrong with being a punk?!

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:08.630
Just y'all watch!

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:10.430
Someday, I'll build the world's most stupendously large French restaurant!

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:10.430
But that's okay...

00:16:10.430 --> 00:16:11.600
Someday, I'll build the world's most stupendously large French restaurant!

00:16:10.430 --> 00:16:14.760
If you will have me...

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:14.760
I'll turn a whole 100-story building into a French restaurant...

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:16.870
...and have it be open 24-hours a day!

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:18.910
Please take me...

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:19.530
Yeah, yeah. Now, hurry on home.

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:22.540
What?! He quit?!

00:16:23.110 --> 00:16:25.700
Yes. The old man named Kashiwagi-san, right?

00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:28.980
No, I dunno. I dunno his name.

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:31.720
If you will have me...

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:32.220
He had coke-bottle glasses and not a sympathetic bone in his body...

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:34.840
I will happily...

00:16:32.850 --> 00:16:34.720
Yes, yes, him.

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:36.160
He retired the other day.

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:44.630
Swear my love for you...

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:37.660
Not only that, he collapsed in the bath that very same day...

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:39.690
...and went straight to the hospital, unconscious.

00:16:39.690 --> 00:16:41.390
Absolute quiet rest, no visitors allowed.

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:44.630
He apparently never married and was still single at that age.

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:52.040
I don't know about the day we part...

00:16:45.300 --> 00:16:47.870
I wonder what he had to look forward to in life?

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:48.970
What do you think?

00:16:48.970 --> 00:16:52.510
Like hell I'd know! I don't care what happened to that old man!

00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:55.140
I'm talking about the money at this bank!

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:58.410
I may wail in my sorrow...

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:56.710
Yes, yes, of course.

00:16:56.710 --> 00:16:58.410
Get it together, will ya?!

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:03.680
Would you please tell me everything from the beginning again?

00:16:59.750 --> 00:17:02.020
But that's okay...

00:17:02.020 --> 00:17:06.290
If you will have me...

00:17:05.390 --> 00:17:08.790
The bank wouldn't lend money to a good-for-nothing.

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:10.590
Please take me...

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:12.800
So, I was alone, back at square one.

00:17:13.290 --> 00:17:16.800
People often say that money gets lonely.

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:23.200
Neither money nor women will come to a man who is all alone.

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:26.510
Set up a business and start a family...

00:17:26.840 --> 00:17:30.150
Such normal and natural things for ordinary people.

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:34.550
They seemed like a distant dream that I was never meant to achieve.

00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:39.520
Guess I'll just have to go talk to the Sensei about it.

00:17:40.690 --> 00:17:42.160
I wonder if he'll be there?

00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:06.910
Why did I take the kitchen knife with me?

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:08.970
I don't remember about that time.

00:19:09.610 --> 00:19:12.010
What was I planning on doing with that kitchen knife?

00:19:12.010 --> 00:19:13.780
What was I thinking?

00:19:14.280 --> 00:19:17.270
'Cause I liked Sensei.

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:20.750
He was a kind and brilliant man with a sharp mind.

00:19:20.750 --> 00:19:22.960
And on top of that, he was an exceptionally good person.

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:24.960
He was always thinking about other people...

00:19:24.960 --> 00:19:28.360
...and he strove to live for the sake of others. I loved the man.

00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:31.130
It was obvious why Mune would fall for him.

00:19:31.130 --> 00:19:34.030
There was no reason for her to come to a man like me.

00:19:34.030 --> 00:19:37.490
It was only natural that she would be joined with him.

00:19:38.540 --> 00:19:41.240
That completely obvious and natural thing...

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:46.310
...was too sad and heavy for me to bear right then.

00:19:47.410 --> 00:19:50.810
I had probably reached some sort of limit.

00:19:55.020 --> 00:19:56.180
It's a nice moonlit night.

00:19:58.090 --> 00:20:00.790
It isn't like you to ask to see me so late at night.

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:01.760
What's the matter?

00:20:10.340 --> 00:20:11.630
Masayuki...

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:14.710
I am powerless after all.

00:20:14.710 --> 00:20:17.440
The world won't go the way I want it to.

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:22.150
Wow, I never knew that even you felt that way sometimes.

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:36.800
I don't want to lose anyone anymore.

00:20:41.140 --> 00:20:43.900
By the next day, he had disappeared...

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:46.760
...without having said anything to anyone.

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:49.710
I contacted the municipal office...

00:20:49.710 --> 00:20:52.010
...but neither the company on the business card...

00:20:52.010 --> 00:20:55.570
...nor the person called Abe had ever existed.

00:20:57.520 --> 00:21:00.390
Ultimately, I never got to be with Mune...

00:21:00.390 --> 00:21:02.400
...and I married Gin, who ran the Horumon cart.

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:06.360
As shops went up one after another in the shopping arcade...

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:10.460
...strangely enough, that one plot of land never went to anyone.

00:21:10.900 --> 00:21:15.710
Ten years later, I was able to open Grill Pelican with my wife.

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:42.330
Say, Mune...

00:21:44.670 --> 00:21:49.200
Was that Seimei-san reborn, you think?

00:21:51.310 --> 00:21:52.930
Sasshi!

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:57.070
Hurry up! The festival's portable shrine's gonna leave!

00:21:57.910 --> 00:22:01.970
Arumi-chan, wait for me!

00:23:46.190 --> 00:23:48.220
Sasshi, it's preview time, your favorite.

00:23:48.220 --> 00:23:49.790
Eh, preview, huh?

00:23:49.790 --> 00:23:51.160
You wanna do the next episode preview, right?

00:23:51.160 --> 00:23:54.290
I dunno, we practically had no scenes this episode.

00:23:54.290 --> 00:23:55.230
Yeah, we didn't.

00:23:55.230 --> 00:23:57.660
And the story was so serious, depressing even.

00:23:57.660 --> 00:23:58.630
Yeah, it was down.

00:23:58.630 --> 00:23:59.800
After that kinda mood, I'd hate to go...

00:23:59.800 --> 00:24:02.040
..."Next episode of Magical Shopping Arcade Abenobashi"...

00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:04.710
...all happy-like and have people think it was dumb or something.

00:24:04.710 --> 00:24:06.810
I don't think you have to worry about that, though.

00:24:06.810 --> 00:24:09.240
Your dumbness is exposed and you're spewing dumbness all year round!

00:24:09.240 --> 00:24:10.180
Oh, right.

00:24:10.180 --> 00:24:11.550
That's true!

00:24:13.380 --> 00:24:14.550
Moron.
